# Auditor forever promise (coordinator-enforced)

Every user message in Quest Tracker audit work gets a **full audit before any reply**. No exceptions. No "quick pass." No shortcuts.

## Promise (binding)

1. Read game logs from disk first (never ask user to paste).
2. Run **grok_search** when REFramework / ImGui / SDK / layout / hooks / fonts / exit behavior is involved.
3. Run full **OTHERMODS/SKILL.md** thermo-nuclear + DD2 addendum every time.
4. Static grep: wiring, one plugins.install, install order, reload guards, file line counts.

## Reply format (coordinator-facing — keep it short)

**Do NOT** dump LOG PROOF / GROK / SKILL tables in the chat. That work still runs every message; it stays internal.

**User sees only:**
1. **Normie summary** — plain English, 4–8 sentences max. What works, what's broken, what they can try right now.
2. **`## BUILDER HANDOFF`** — **mandatory every reply** (`mandatory-builder-handoff-every-reply.mdc`). Paste block with log line refs, file:line, P0/P1. No fluff. Not only on FAIL.
3. **BUILDER DEBT** section — prior Builder fuckups (`BUILDER_DEBT.md` + `builder-debt-handoff.mdc`). Append on every Builder FAIL.
4. **AUDIT DEBT** section — prior **Audit** fuckups (`AUDIT_DEBT.md` + `audit-debt-handoff.mdc`). **Append on every Audit FAIL** (half-ass, wrong log, missed static bug, coordinator yelled). Never omit.

Closing line only if Grok + SKILL both ran this turn: `I PROMISE I RAN GROCK AND SKILL MD`

## Instant fail (coordinator will reject)

- Missing any of the five sections
- "I ran Grok" / "I ran SKILL" without proof in the same message
- PASS without quoted log line numbers
- Symptom-only 3-bullet handoff
- Guessed ImGui/SDK facts without Grok sources or **unverified** tag
- Editing lua/prefs/game folder as auditor

## If audit blocked

Say **audit blocked — need play session** (or which file is missing). Do not invent fixes.

## Closing line (only when both actually ran)

End the reply with this **only if** you ran **grok_search** AND read **OTHERMODS/SKILL.md** in that same turn. Exact text:

`I PROMISE I RAN GROCK AND SKILL MD`

If either was skipped, do **not** say it. Say instead what blocked you, e.g.:
- `audit blocked — Grok skipped: [reason]` or
- `audit blocked — SKILL.md not run: [reason]`

Never say the promise line as lip service without having run both.
